---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="about — TinkSoft">
  <h1>about</h1>
  <p>
    Hi, I'm Tink. TinkSoft is where I build software in public.
  </p>
  <p>
    Building in public means sharing the whole process — the wins, the bugs
    that ate a weekend, the architecture decisions I'll regret in six months.
    Writing it down keeps me honest and keeps me shipping.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every post in the <a href="/">build log</a> is a real update from a real
    project. No polish, no marketing. Just what happened.
  </p>
  <h2>why the 90s look?</h2>
  <p>
    Because the old web was fast, honest, and built by people making things
    for the fun of it. This site is plain HTML, ships zero JavaScript, and
    loads instantly on anything. That felt right.
  </p>
  <h2>link to me</h2>
  <p>
    <img src="/badge.svg" width="88" height="31" alt="TINKSOFT 88x31 button" />
    — a classic 88&times;31 button, like the old web intended. Grab it:
  </p>
  <div class="content"><pre>&lt;a href="https://tinksoft.com"&gt;&lt;img
  src="https://tinksoft.com/badge.svg"
  width="88" height="31" alt="TINKSOFT"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;</pre></div>
  <h2>get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    Email: <a href="mailto:talmage.m.lewis@gmail.com">talmage.m.lewis@gmail.com</a>
  </p>
</Base>
